## In-language `test "..." { ... }` blocks — Aether's first-class testing
## syntax. Tests are functions with `{Throw}` effect; failing `assert`s throw.

fn add(x: Int, y: Int) -> Int effects {} { x + y }

fn double(x: Int) -> Int effects {} { x + x }

test "add is commutative" {
  assert_eq(add(2, 3), add(3, 2))
}

test "double matches add" {
  assert_eq(double(7), add(7, 7))
}

test "comparison" {
  assert(1 < 2)
  assert(2 <= 2)
  assert(3 > 2)
}

fn main() -> Unit effects {} {
  ()
}
